Embercall Industries is a corporation. [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]] operates under its corporate banner.

The company is small and was only founded a few months ago; no owner is named on paper, and it is held by a second, private corporation that paid to keep its own details out of reach. Its recorded headquarters is P.O. Box 9C at the [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center.

The radar dish [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] took from the roof of the roller rink was made by Embercall, and the signal it received appeared to come from the Gryphonline distribution center as well.

It is one of a set: [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]] has the local gangs mount dishes like it on rooftops across the poorer districts, over places where crowds gather.

[[Aut]] says the Embercall is a derivative of the [[Voidsong]], and that [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] has to do with it.

The radar dish network Tywelwyn was building is tied to [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]]; his notes point to the Embercall as the source of its hardware.

Embercall first appears in the newspapers a little under two years ago, some six months after the [[Voidsong]] was first heard, in the first reports of the wall of fire around [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]]. Only a small part of the government's rescue parties came back out through the flame, and those who did spoke of the Embercall and died soon after. A radio communications company named Embercall Incorporated also ran a hiring notice in the listings about a year ago.
